```

As we can see in the function where tx is initiated only the `amount` is taken from the user, without any additional tokens to be used as gas fees. Furthermore, the `ERC20TransferPayload` that is decoded in the destination chain for the `ChakraSettlementHandler` to know how many tokens to unlock/mint to the `to` recipient also uses the exact same `amount` that is provided as an argument without deducting gas fees from it. After that on the destination, the `receive_cross_chain_msg` payload is decoded as is and the same whole amount is given to the user:

[ChakraSettlementHandler.sol](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-08-chakra/blob/main/solidity/handler/contracts/ChakraSettlementHandler.sol#L300C14-L352)

```solidity
