In the end, validators are the ones that cover all the destination gas fees and users only pay the source execution. At some point, validators will refuse to perform their duties. They will stop signing messages, which means the protocol will become DoSsed until another group of validators is set, but this is a temporary solution since they also will have to pay for the gas.

The same flaw is in the `Cairo` contracts, `handler_erc20` doesn’t take any fees from the users, encode the payload in the same way, and in his `receive_cross_chain_msg` uses the whole amount that has been encoded. Basically, the exact same issue is in the `Cairo` contracts.

